# Delivery Tracking

- GitHub Project #4 is the delivery-tracking source of truth.
- Use Version = iteration, GitHub Issue = meaningful unit of work, and only Planned / In Progress / Done statuses.
- Before meaningful implementation, check for an existing issue. Create a focused issue when needed and link it to its version issue.
- Move work to In Progress when implementation begins. After verification and required documentation updates, reference the issue in the commit or PR, move it to Done, and close it.
- Keep completed V1, V1.5, and V2 as their existing high-level issues. Do not reconstruct their individual history.
- Keep V3 current, V4 upcoming, and V5 future. Do not implement V4 or V5 work until the iteration is started.
- Split scope only when it is independently meaningful; do not create issues for classes, methods, or trivial edits.
